A) IN-MEMORY OBJECT CACHE SYSTEM (VFS-LIKE MODEL)
================================================================================

Your program simulates Linux kernel cache mechanisms like:
- inode cache
- dentry cache

WHAT IT DOES IN REAL WORLD:
----------------------------------------
✔ Caches metadata of files and objects in RAM
✔ Avoids repeated slow disk access
✔ Speeds up file system operations drastically

YOUR PROGRAM MAPPING:
----------------------------------------
- SLAB = fast object allocation (inode-like objects)
- Hash table = quick lookup (filename → inode mapping style)
- RCU = safe concurrent access
- Shrinker = memory reclaim under pressure

REAL WORLD USAGE:
----------------------------------------
- File systems (ext4, xfs, btrfs)
- High-performance storage engines
- Database buffer caches

PRACTICAL SYSTEM NAME:
----------------------------------------
"High-Speed In-Memory Metadata Cache Engine"

